        "Content": "Superb 4 Bedroom Semi-Detached Family Home Overlooking Large Green Area – Extension - South Facing Rear Garden – Prime Mornington Location\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to acquire this beautifully presented 4-bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally located within the highly sought-after Mornington Court development, an exclusive residential development of just 90 houses with the added benefit of an onsite crèche. \r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned overlooking a large communal green area, this superb home offers spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout, ideal for modern family living. The property also benefits from a sun-drenched south-facing rear garden, excellent storage, and a highly convenient location close to every conceivable amenity.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nGround Floor\r\nEntrance Hall: Inviting entrance hall with porcelain floor tiles and under-stairs storage.\r\nGuest Bathroom: Ground floor guest bathroom with window and porcelain floor tiling.\r\nKitchen: Bright and spacious kitchen featuring Porcelain floor tiles, Recessed lighting, Generous countertop workspace and Ample fitted storage presses.\r\nUtility Room: Plumbed separate utility room offering additional storage and laundry space.\r\nDining Area: Well-proportioned dining area with recessed lighting, Porcelain floor tiles and access to extension.\r\nExtension: Excellent additional living space featuring porcelain floor tiles, Velux window and direct access to rear garden.\r\nLiving Room: Spacious separate living room with Semi-solid wood flooring and multi-burner stove. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nMaster Bedroom: Wood flooring and 4 built-in wardrobes.\r\nEnsuite: Fully tiled with shower cubicle and Triton shower.\r\nBedroom 2: Double bedroom with wood flooring and 2 built-in wardrobes.\r\nMain Bathroom: Skylight, Bath and  Shower connection.\r\nBedroom 3: Double bedroom with wood flooring and 2 built-in wardrobes.\r\nBedroom 4: Large single bedroom with wood flooring and 2 half built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nAdditional features include: Attic access and hot press.  \r\n\r\nOutside\r\nFront: Driveway with lawn area and off-street parking. \r\nRear: South-facing back garden, fully concreted, gated side entrance, garden shed with electricity and fuse board. \r\n\r\nPrime Location & Excellent Amenities\r\nFamilies will appreciate that The Grange Preschool & Afterschool Club is just a two-minute walk away, making school runs effortless.\r\n\r\nTransport\r\nDrogheda Train Station and Laytown Train Station (Park & Ride) with frequent services to Dublin Connolly, Drogheda and beyond.\r\nEasy access to the M1 motorway, placing Dublin City Centre and Dublin Airport within convenient reach.\r\nLocal bus routes and Matthews Bus services to Dublin, Drogheda and Dundalk.\r\nD1 and D2 bus stop just 250 meters away via a pedestrian gate, providing easy access to Drogheda, Bettystown and Dublin. Matthews Bus services to Dublin, Drogheda and Dundalk.\r\n\r\nHealthcare\r\nHSE Primary Health Centre\r\nOur Lady of Lourdes Hospital, Drogheda\r\n\r\nDining & Leisure\r\nEnjoy an excellent local food scene including Navy Café, The Village Hotel, Duende, and Matt the Thrasher Gastropub, along with numerous cafés, takeaways and traditional pubs.\r\n\r\nSports & Recreation\r\nLaytown & Bettystown Golf Club – superb 18-hole links course.\r\nFitness clubs, swimming pool, boxing, rugby, football, GAA, athletics, hockey and running clubs.\r\nScenic coastal walks and cycling routes throughout the Boyne Valley.\r\n\r\nShopping\r\nNearby shopping options include Tesco, Lidl, Aldi, Dunnes Stores, SuperValu, MACE and Mr Price, while Drogheda offers extensive retail options just minutes away. Harry’s Centra and petrol station is also only a short drive away.\r\n\r\nLocal Services\r\nPost office, veterinary clinics, butcher, pharmacies, hardware stores and an excellent range of pre-school, primary and secondary schools are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment only.\r\n\r\nPlease note: All details, descriptions and photographs are for guidance purposes only."
